cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it as below. The method comes from the
  doctoral thesis of Jan Horn listed under references; please cite it as well.
type: software
title: "Surface velocity from a single multi-flash image"
abstract: >-
  Direction and speed of a moving textured surface from one multi-flash camera
  image, using the 2-D FFT and the Radon transform. Python package fftvel and
  MATLAB/Octave package +fftvel; parity tests in Python and GNU Octave check
  that both give the same results to 1e-9. Tested in simulation and on
  synthetic image sequences; not yet on real multi-flash images.
authors:
  - family-names: Neumann
    given-names: Oliver
version: 0.1.0
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/onewmann/2D-FFT-Code"
keywords:
  - multi-flash
  - multiple exposure
  - stroboscopic imaging
  - velocimetry
  - speed over ground
  - velocity measurement
  - machine vision
  - signal processing
  - FFT
  - Radon transform
  - Python
  - MATLAB
  - GNU Octave
